\n.pi/\n\n.idea/\n=== is bin/rick tracked? ===\nbin/rick\n=== git status --short ===\n M .rick/domain/project-conventions.md\n M .rick/dream/prompts/dream_prompt.md\n M .rick/dream/prompts/skill_gen_loop.md\n M .rick/dream/prompts/skill_sense.md\n M .rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tasks.json\n M .rick/loops/tdd-red-green-refactor-loop.md\n M bin/rick\n?? .rick/draft/loops/loop_6/\n?? \".rick/draft/rfc/rfc-rick-\\344\\270\\211\\345\\261\\202\\346\\236\\266\\346\\236\\204\\351\\207\\215\\346\\236\\204\\344\\270\\216spec\\344\\277\\241\\346\\201\\257\\345\\206\\205\\346\\240\\270-2026-08-14.md\"\n?? .rick/dream/prompts/skill_gen_domain.md\n?? .rick/jobs/job_32/\n?? .rick/jobs/job_33/doing/prompts/\n?? .rick/jobs/job_33/doing/session_id\n?? .rick/jobs/job_33/doing/tasks.json\n?? .rick/jobs/job_34/doing/\n?? .rick/jobs/job_35/doing/prompts/\n?? .rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tasks/\n?? .rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tests/\n?? .rick/jobs/job_35/plan/\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786906873998},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`bin/rick` IS tracked in git (git ls-files shows it). And `.gitignore` has `bin/`. So `bin/rick` is tracked but `bin/` is in gitignore. There's already a modified `bin/rick` (M bin/rick) from a previous build.\n\nThe test method says `go build -o bin/rick ./cmd/rick`. But to avoid polluting the tracked `bin/rick`, and given the existing convention (task5 builds to temp dir), I should build to a temp directory and use that binary for the CLI checks.\n\nWait, but the test method explicitly says `go build -o bin/rick ./cmd/rick` and then uses `./bin/rick`. Let me think about what's best:\n\nOption A: Follow the test method literally — build to `bin/rick` (overwrites tracked file, causes git diff). Then run `./bin/rick` for CLI checks.\n\nOption B: Build to a temp dir (like task5) and use that binary. This avoids polluting `bin/rick`.\n\nThe test method's intent is \"build the binary and test the CLI behaviors\". The exact output path `bin/ri